{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Hotkeys provides three Vue composables for tracking live keyboard state: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useHeldKeys"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useHeldKeyCodes"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useKeyHold"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"useheldkeys","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useHeldKeys"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<script setup lang=\"ts\">\nimport { useHeldKeys } from '@tanstack/vue-hotkeys'\n\nconst heldKeys = useHeldKeys()\n</script>\n\n<template>\n  <div>{{ heldKeys.length > 0 ? heldKeys.join(' + ') : 'No keys held' }}</div>\n</template>","lang":"vue"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"useheldkeycodes","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useHeldKeyCodes"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<script setup lang=\"ts\">\nimport { useHeldKeyCodes } from '@tanstack/vue-hotkeys'\n\nconst heldCodes = useHeldKeyCodes()\n</script>","lang":"vue"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"usekeyhold","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useKeyHold"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<script setup lang=\"ts\">\nimport { useKeyHold } from '@tanstack/vue-hotkeys'\n\nconst isShiftHeld = useKeyHold('Shift')\n</script>\n\n<template>\n  <span :class=\"{ active: isShiftHeld }\">Shift</span>\n</template>","lang":"vue"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"common-patterns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Common patterns"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"hold-to-reveal-ui","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Hold-to-reveal UI"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<script setup lang=\"ts\">\nimport { useKeyHold } from '@tanstack/vue-hotkeys'\n\nconst isShiftHeld = useKeyHold('Shift')\n</script>\n\n<template>\n  <button v-if=\"isShiftHeld\">Permanently Delete</button>\n  <button v-else>Move to Trash</button>\n</template>","lang":"vue"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"debugging-key-display","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Debugging key display"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<script setup lang=\"ts\">\nimport {\n  formatForDisplay,\n  useHeldKeyCodes,\n  useHeldKeys,\n} from '@tanstack/vue-hotkeys'\nimport type { RegisterableHotkey } from '@tanstack/vue-hotkeys'\n\nconst heldKeys = useHeldKeys()\nconst heldCodes = useHeldKeyCodes()\n</script>\n\n<template>\n  <div v-for=\"key in heldKeys\" :key=\"key\">\n    <strong>{{\n      formatForDisplay(key as RegisterableHotkey, { useSymbols: true })\n    }}</strong>\n    <span>{{ heldCodes[key] }}</span>\n  </div>\n</template>","lang":"vue"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"under-the-hood","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Under the hood"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"All three composables subscribe to the singleton "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"KeyStateTracker"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { getKeyStateTracker } from '@tanstack/vue-hotkeys'\n\nconst tracker = getKeyStateTracker()\ntracker.getHeldKeys()\ntracker.isKeyHeld('Shift')","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"modifier-held-shortcut-hints","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Modifier-held shortcut hints"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useHotkeyHint"},{"type":"text","value":" answers whether held modifiers are relevant to a binding. Keep formatting and badge styling in your component:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const visible = useHotkeyHint(() => binding.value) // computed ref: visible.value","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Alt+Shift+[KeyK]"},{"type":"text","value":", holding Alt, Shift, or both reveals the hint. An extra Control hides it; releasing all modifiers or blurring the window hides it. Nonmodifier keys are ignored. AltGraph does not reveal hints. Pass "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ exact: true }"},{"type":"text","value":" to require all binding modifiers, or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ platform: 'mac' }"},{"type":"text","value":" to resolve Mod explicitly. Supply the same platform used by the registration when overriding detection."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Combine the boolean with the action's enabled state. The helper does not register a shortcut or determine whether its target is focused. The core equivalent is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"matchesHeldModifiers(binding, heldKeys, options)"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"useheldkeys","text":"useHeldKeys","level":2},{"id":"useheldkeycodes","text":"useHeldKeyCodes","level":2},{"id":"usekeyhold","text":"useKeyHold","level":2},{"id":"common-patterns","text":"Common patterns","level":2},{"id":"hold-to-reveal-ui","text":"Hold-to-reveal UI","level":3},{"id":"debugging-key-display","text":"Debugging key display","level":3},{"id":"under-the-hood","text":"Under the hood","level":2},{"id":"modifier-held-shortcut-hints","text":"Modifier-held shortcut hints","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nTanStack Hotkeys provides three Vue composables for tracking live keyboard state: `useHeldKeys`, `useHeldKeyCodes`, and `useKeyHold`.\n\n## `useHeldKeys`\n\n```vue\n<script setup lang=\"ts\">\nimport { useHeldKeys } from '@tanstack/vue-hotkeys'\n\nconst heldKeys = useHeldKeys()\n</script>\n\n<template>\n  <div>{{ heldKeys.length > 0 ? heldKeys.join(' + ') : 'No keys held' }}</div>\n</template>\n```\n\n## `useHeldKeyCodes`\n\n```vue\n<script setup lang=\"ts\">\nimport { useHeldKeyCodes } from '@tanstack/vue-hotkeys'\n\nconst heldCodes = useHeldKeyCodes()\n</script>\n```\n\n## `useKeyHold`\n\n```vue\n<script setup lang=\"ts\">\nimport { useKeyHold } from '@tanstack/vue-hotkeys'\n\nconst isShiftHeld = useKeyHold('Shift')\n</script>\n\n<template>\n  <span :class=\"{ active: isShiftHeld }\">Shift</span>\n</template>\n```\n\n## Common patterns\n\n### Hold-to-reveal UI\n\n```vue\n<script setup lang=\"ts\">\nimport { useKeyHold } from '@tanstack/vue-hotkeys'\n\nconst isShiftHeld = useKeyHold('Shift')\n</script>\n\n<template>\n  <button v-if=\"isShiftHeld\">Permanently Delete</button>\n  <button v-else>Move to Trash</button>\n</template>\n```\n\n### Debugging key display\n\n```vue\n<script setup lang=\"ts\">\nimport {\n  formatForDisplay,\n  useHeldKeyCodes,\n  useHeldKeys,\n} from '@tanstack/vue-hotkeys'\nimport type { RegisterableHotkey } from '@tanstack/vue-hotkeys'\n\nconst heldKeys = useHeldKeys()\nconst heldCodes = useHeldKeyCodes()\n</script>\n\n<template>\n  <div v-for=\"key in heldKeys\" :key=\"key\">\n    <strong>{{\n      formatForDisplay(key as RegisterableHotkey, { useSymbols: true })\n    }}</strong>\n    <span>{{ heldCodes[key] }}</span>\n  </div>\n</template>\n```\n\n## Under the hood\n\nAll three composables subscribe to the singleton `KeyStateTracker`:\n\n```ts\nimport { getKeyStateTracker } from '@tanstack/vue-hotkeys'\n\nconst tracker = getKeyStateTracker()\ntracker.getHeldKeys()\ntracker.isKeyHeld('Shift')\n```\n\n## Modifier-held shortcut hints\n\n`useHotkeyHint` answers whether held modifiers are relevant to a binding. Keep formatting and badge styling in your component:\n\n```ts\nconst visible = useHotkeyHint(() => binding.value) // computed ref: visible.value\n```\n\nFor `Alt+Shift+[KeyK]`, holding Alt, Shift, or both reveals the hint. An extra Control hides it; releasing all modifiers or blurring the window hides it. Nonmodifier keys are ignored. AltGraph does not reveal hints. Pass `{ exact: true }` to require all binding modifiers, or `{ platform: 'mac' }` to resolve Mod explicitly. Supply the same platform used by the registration when overriding detection.\n\nCombine the boolean with the action's enabled state. The helper does not register a shortcut or determine whether its target is focused. The core equivalent is `matchesHeldModifiers(binding, heldKeys, options)`.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Key State Tracking Guide\nid: key-state-tracking\n---\n\nTanStack Hotkeys provides three Vue composables for tracking live keyboard state: `useHeldKeys`, `useHeldKeyCodes`, and `useKeyHold`.\n\n## `useHeldKeys`\n\n```vue\n<script setup lang=\"ts\">\nimport { useHeldKeys } from '@tanstack/vue-hotkeys'\n\nconst heldKeys = useHeldKeys()\n</script>\n\n<template>\n  <div>{{ heldKeys.length > 0 ? heldKeys.join(' + ') : 'No keys held' }}</div>\n</template>\n```\n\n## `useHeldKeyCodes`\n\n```vue\n<script setup lang=\"ts\">\nimport { useHeldKeyCodes } from '@tanstack/vue-hotkeys'\n\nconst heldCodes = useHeldKeyCodes()\n</script>\n```\n\n## `useKeyHold`\n\n```vue\n<script setup lang=\"ts\">\nimport { useKeyHold } from '@tanstack/vue-hotkeys'\n\nconst isShiftHeld = useKeyHold('Shift')\n</script>\n\n<template>\n  <span :class=\"{ active: isShiftHeld }\">Shift</span>\n</template>\n```\n\n## Common patterns\n\n### Hold-to-reveal UI\n\n```vue\n<script setup lang=\"ts\">\nimport { useKeyHold } from '@tanstack/vue-hotkeys'\n\nconst isShiftHeld = useKeyHold('Shift')\n</script>\n\n<template>\n  <button v-if=\"isShiftHeld\">Permanently Delete</button>\n  <button v-else>Move to Trash</button>\n</template>\n```\n\n### Debugging key display\n\n```vue\n<script setup lang=\"ts\">\nimport {\n  formatForDisplay,\n  useHeldKeyCodes,\n  useHeldKeys,\n} from '@tanstack/vue-hotkeys'\nimport type { RegisterableHotkey } from '@tanstack/vue-hotkeys'\n\nconst heldKeys = useHeldKeys()\nconst heldCodes = useHeldKeyCodes()\n</script>\n\n<template>\n  <div v-for=\"key in heldKeys\" :key=\"key\">\n    <strong>{{\n      formatForDisplay(key as RegisterableHotkey, { useSymbols: true })\n    }}</strong>\n    <span>{{ heldCodes[key] }}</span>\n  </div>\n</template>\n```\n\n## Under the hood\n\nAll three composables subscribe to the singleton `KeyStateTracker`:\n\n```ts\nimport { getKeyStateTracker } from '@tanstack/vue-hotkeys'\n\nconst tracker = getKeyStateTracker()\ntracker.getHeldKeys()\ntracker.isKeyHeld('Shift')\n```\n\n## Modifier-held shortcut hints\n\n`useHotkeyHint` answers whether held modifiers are relevant to a binding. Keep formatting and badge styling in your component:\n\n```ts\nconst visible = useHotkeyHint(() => binding.value) // computed ref: visible.value\n```\n\nFor `Alt+Shift+[KeyK]`, holding Alt, Shift, or both reveals the hint. An extra Control hides it; releasing all modifiers or blurring the window hides it. Nonmodifier keys are ignored. AltGraph does not reveal hints. Pass `{ exact: true }` to require all binding modifiers, or `{ platform: 'mac' }` to resolve Mod explicitly. Supply the same platform used by the registration when overriding detection.\n\nCombine the boolean with the action's enabled state. The helper does not register a shortcut or determine whether its target is focused. The core equivalent is `matchesHeldModifiers(binding, heldKeys, options)`.\n"}
